From c205adf2a273b2098b75b10616454d8b2832dff9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:13:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Debug flag: count non-finite TileLang gate inputs instead of
 trapping

With SPARK3_DEBUG_ROUTER_NONFINITE=1 each TileLang gate router counts the
rows whose input or gate logits are non-finite, split into routed and
masked rows, records the first routed one and its batch size, and zeroes
the logits so the step completes. Probes count non-finite rows at each
decoder layer's attention input and output, FFN input and residual, inside
attention (qr, kv, q, MQA output) and in the DSpark drafter (input
embeddings, main_x, context KV). Every check takes the next value of one
device counter, so the earliest first-bad sequence marks the origin. The
model runner logs the counts after graph capture and after the DSpark
cost profile. Off by default.
